    "title": "Korean Keyboard Online Free — Type 한국어 키보드 | WriteWithin",
    "meta_description": "Type Korean (한국어 키보드) online free with a virtual keyboard. Use physical keys or on-screen layout, phonetic/IME input when available, emoji, copy, speak, practice phrases, and private local drafts. No install.",
    "h1": "Korean Keyboard",
    "intro": "Type 한국어 instantly in your browser. Switch layouts, use phonetic or IME input when available, insert emoji, copy your text, or practice common phrases. Hangul jamo combine into syllables as you type.",
    "body_html": "<h2>How to type Korean online</h2>\n<p>Use the Standard 두벌식 layout: consonants and vowels combine into Hangul syllables automatically (ㄱ+ㅏ→가). Shift for double jamo (ㄲ, ㄸ, ㅃ, ㅆ, ㅉ). Esc toggles English. Sebeolsik is listed for learners exploring layouts.</p>\n<h2>Why use a Korean virtual keyboard?</h2>\n<p>Shared computers, travel laptops, and borrowed devices often lack the right input method. WriteWithin gives you a private, install-free Korean keyboard with modern mobile support, romanization hints, and text-to-speech.</p>\n<h2>Tips for Korean writers and learners</h2>\n<p>Type continuously — finals move to the next syllable when you start a new vowel (เช่น 한 + ㄱ + ㅏ → 한가). Use Practice for 안녕하세요.</p>"
  },
  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "How does Hangul composition work here?",
      "answer": "Each key inserts a jamo. The engine composes initial+medial(+final) into a syllable block as you type, including complex vowels like ㅘ and double finals like ㄳ."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do I need to install a Korean keyboard?",
      "answer": "No. WriteWithin’s Korean keyboard runs entirely in your browser. Type, copy, and paste into any app — nothing to install."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I use my physical keyboard for Korean?",
      "answer": "Yes. The on-screen layout shows which physical key maps to each character. Press Esc to switch between English and Korean mode."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is my text private?",
      "answer": "Yes. Typing stays on your device. We do not upload what you type to our servers."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does the Korean keyboard work on mobile?",
      "answer": "Yes. The keyboard adapts for touch screens with large targets, emoji, and a sticky editor on phones and tablets."
    }
  ],
